  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `endRewards` function in `Launchpad.sol` calculates the Uniswap V2 pair address using the `pairFor` function, which computes the address based on `token0`, `token1`, and `uniV2InitCodeHash`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction pairFor(address factory, address tokenA, address tokenB) internal view returns (IUniswapV2Pair pair) {\n    (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n    pair = IUniswapV2Pair(\n        address(\n            uint160(\n                uint256(\n                    keccak256(\n                        abi.encodePacked(\n                            hex\"ff\",\n                            factory,\n                            keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1)),\n                            uniV2InitCodeHash\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        )\n    );\n}\n```\n\nHowever, the `createPair` function in `GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol` uses a different `salt` that includes `_launchpadLp` and `_launchpadFeeDistributor`:\n\n```solidity\nbytes32 salt = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, _launchpadLp, _launchpadFeeDistributor));\nassembly {\n    pair := create2(0, add(bytecode, 32), mload(bytecode), salt)\n}\n```\n\nThis discrepancy in the `salt` calculation causes the pair address computed by `pairFor` to always differ from the actual pair address created by `createPair` during the `_createPairAndSwapRemaining` function in `Launchpad.sol` when a token launch graduates. As a result, the `endRewards` function, which calls `distributor.endRewards(pair)`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction endRewards() external onlyLaunchAsset {\n    address quote = _launches[msg.sender].quote;\n    IGTELaunchpadV2Pair pair = IGTELaunchpadV2Pair(address(pairFor(address(uniV2Factory), msg.sender, quote)));\n    distributor.endRewards(pair);\n}\n```\n\nalways reverts due to an invalid pair address, preventing the protocol from terminating the rewards accrual process for a launched token.\n\n**Impact**:  \nThis vulnerability causes a Denial of Service (DoS) for the `endRewards` function, a critical protocol feature intended to stop rewards accrual (e.g., when `totalFeeShare` reaches zero in `LaunchToken.sol`). The issue affects all token launches, as the incorrect pair address calculation is inherent to the `pairFor` function. This disrupts the protocol's ability to manage rewards, undermining its core functionality and reliability. According to Code4rena guidelines, this qualifies as a **High** severity issue due to its direct impact on a critical protocol function without requiring user error or specific conditions.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n1. **Align `pairFor` with `createPair` Salt Calculation**:\n   Update the `pairFor` function in `Launchpad.sol` to include `_launchpadLp` and `_launchpadFeeDistributor` in the `salt` calculation, matching the logic in `GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.createPair`",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {LaunchpadTestBase} from \"./LaunchpadTestBase.sol\";\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport {IUniswapV2Factory} from \"@gte-univ2-core/interfaces/IUniswapV2Factory.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\nimport {Launchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol\";\nimport {console} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is LaunchpadTestBase {\n    /**\n     * PoC demonstrating that endRewards reverts due to incorrect pair address calculation\n     */\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        // Setup user\n        address user = makeAddr(\"user\");\n        deal(address(quoteToken), user, type(uint256).max);\n\n        // User buys all base tokens + 1 to trigger graduation\n        uint256 maxBase = launchpad.launches(token).curve.bondingSupply(token);\n        uint256 amountOutBase = maxBase + 1 ether; // Buy all + 1 to exhaust bonding supply\n        uint256 maxAmountInQuote = launchpad.quoteQuoteForBase(token, amountOutBase, true);\n        ILaunchpad.BuyData memory buyData = ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n            token: token,\n            recipient: user,\n            amountOutBase: amountOutBase,\n            maxAmountInQuote: maxAmountInQuote,\n            account: user\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(user);\n        launchpad.buy(buyData);\n\n        // Verify graduation occurred and pair was created\n        address factory = address(uniV2Router.factory());\n        address actualPair = IUniswapV2Factory(factory).getPair(token, address(quoteToken));\n        assertTrue(actualPair != address(0), \"Pair should exist after graduation\");\n        assertFalse(launchpad.launches(token).active, \"Bonding should be inactive after graduation\");\n\n        // Verify user's bonding share\n        uint256 userBondingShare = LaunchToken(token).bondingShare(user);\n        assertEq(userBondingShare, maxBase, \"User bonding share should match maxBase\");\n\n        // Directly call endRewards as LaunchToken to simulate _endRewards call\n        vm.prank(token); // Impersonate LaunchToken as msg.sender\n        vm.expectRevert(); // Expect revert due to incorrect pair address\n        Launchpad(address(launchpad)).endRewards();\n\n        // Verify bonding is still inactive (endRewards failed)\n        assertFalse(launchpad.launches(token).active, \"Bonding should remain inactive\");\n    }\n}\n```",
